IMPORT prelude

-- Executive Condominium Housing Scheme Act 1996 (Singapore) -- ss 3, 4, 8 and
-- 10 to 13.
--
-- The rest of the Act, after the eligibility, transfer and acquisition rules in
-- ec-act.l4. The substance here is s 8: what happens to the home when the owner
-- DIES within 10 years of the temporary occupation permit. Three separate
-- clocks run, and missing any of them can vest the home in the Board.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 14 (the Minister's general power), and the compensation and
-- High Court deposit machinery in s 8(6).

§ `Executive Condominium Housing Scheme Act 1996 -- sections 3, 4, 8 and 10 to 13`

§§ `3 -- The scheme, and where the real conditions live`

-- s 3(1): "The Minister MAY establish an executive condominium scheme to
-- provide housing accommodation to such class of persons as the Minister may
-- determine."
--
-- s 3(2): the regulation power, and the list is worth reading because it shows
-- how little of the scheme is in the Act. Regulations may prescribe --
--   (a) the terms and conditions of sale;
--   (b) THE PERSONS TO WHOM housing may be sold, "including but not limited to
--       the QUALIFICATIONS AS TO INCOME, the MINIMUM SIZE OF THE FAMILY,
--       CITIZENSHIP of and OWNERSHIP OF ANY OTHER PROPERTIES by all or any such
--       persons"; and
--   (c) a PENALTY for non-compliance with ss 5 and 9, payable "IN LIEU OF any
--       action which may be taken against the person under any of those
--       provisions".
--
-- So income, family size, citizenship and other property holdings -- the things
-- an applicant would call the eligibility rules -- are all in regulations that
-- were not retrieved. s 5(1)(d) then makes a breach of those regulations a
-- disqualifying ground in its own right, which is how they bind.
DECLARE PrescribedMatter IS ONE OF
    `the terms and conditions of sale`                      -- s 3(2)(a)
    `qualifications as to income`                           -- s 3(2)(b)
    `the minimum size of the family`                        -- s 3(2)(b)
    `citizenship of the purchasers`                         -- s 3(2)(b)
    `ownership of any other properties`                     -- s 3(2)(b)
    `a penalty in lieu of action under section 5 or 9`      -- s 3(2)(c)
    `something stated in the Act itself`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A PrescribedMatter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter is left to regulations rather than stated in the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `something stated in the Act itself` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(2)(c): the prescribed penalty is payable "IN LIEU OF any action which may
-- be taken against the person" under s 5 or s 9. So paying it is an alternative
-- to losing the home, not an addition to it.
GIVEN `a penalty has been prescribed under section 3(2)(c) for the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the penalty has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `action under section 5 or 9 is displaced by payment of the penalty` IF
        `a penalty has been prescribed under section 3(2)(c) for the breach`
    AND `the penalty has been paid`

§§ `4 -- Developers`

-- s 4(1): the Minister may appoint developers to develop specified land and to
-- sell housing under the scheme. s 4(2): the appointment "MUST be published in
-- the Gazette." A condition of the appointment being effective, not a courtesy.
GIVEN `the Minister appointed the developer` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the appointment was published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer is duly appointed` IF
        `the Minister appointed the developer`
    AND `the appointment was published in the Gazette`

§§ `8 -- Death of the owner within 10 years of the permit`

-- s 8(1): a transmission on death, "whether TESTATE OR INTESTATE", or any
-- transfer by the personal representatives, "WITHIN 10 YEARS of the date of
-- issue of the temporary occupation permit ... MUST NOT BE REGISTERED under the
-- Land Titles Act 1993 WITHOUT THE MINISTER'S PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT."
--
-- So the family cannot inherit the title without asking. A will makes no
-- difference.
DECLARE DeathOfOwner HAS
    `the owner has died`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the death or transfer is within 10 years of the temporary occupation permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister gave prior written consent to the transmission or transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(3)(a)
    `representation was taken out within 12 months from the death` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(3)(b)
    `the personal representatives applied for consent within 6 months from the date of representation` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(3)(c)
    `the transmission or transfer was effected within the period the Minister specified` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(2)
    `the Minister refused consent`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 8(4)
    `written notice of the intention to lodge was served`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice stated the compensation and a lodging date at least 28 days after service` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8 applies` IF
        `the facts`'s `the owner has died`
    AND `the facts`'s `the death or transfer is within 10 years of the temporary occupation permit`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transmission may not be registered` IF
        `section 8 applies` `the facts`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the Minister gave prior written consent to the transmission or transfer`

-- s 8(3): THREE SEPARATE CLOCKS, any one of which lets the Minister vest the
-- home in the Board --
--   (a) no representation taken out within 12 MONTHS from the death;
--   (b) representation taken out, but no application for consent within
--       6 MONTHS from the date of representation; or
--   (c) consent obtained, but the transmission not effected within the period
--       the Minister specified.
--
-- A family that probates promptly and then waits seven months before writing to
-- the Minister loses the home on limb (b), having complied with limb (a).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (a) of section 8(3) is made out` IF
    NOT `the facts`'s `representation was taken out within 12 months from the death`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (b) of section 8(3) is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `representation was taken out within 12 months from the death`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the personal representatives applied for consent within 6 months from the date of representation`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (c) of section 8(3) is made out` IF
        `the facts`'s `the Minister gave prior written consent to the transmission or transfer`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the transmission or transfer was effected within the period the Minister specified`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground to vest the home in the Board arises` IF
        `the facts`'s `the Minister refused consent`
    ..  `limb (a) of section 8(3) is made out` `the facts`
    ..  `limb (b) of section 8(3) is made out` `the facts`
    OR  `limb (c) of section 8(3) is made out` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may lodge an instrument vesting the home in the Board` IF
        `section 8 applies` `the facts`
    AND `a ground to vest the home in the Board arises` `the facts`

-- s 8(4): before lodging, the Minister MUST serve written notice on the
-- personal representatives and on all persons known or believed to have an
-- interest, stating the compensation and a lodging date "NOT BEING A DATE
-- EARLIER THAN 28 DAYS after the date the notice is served."
`the minimum notice period before lodging, in days` MEANS 28

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 8(4) notice requirements are met` IF
        `the facts`'s `written notice of the intention to lodge was served`
    AND `the facts`'s `the notice stated the compensation and a lodging date at least 28 days after service`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DeathOfOwner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may lawfully lodge the instrument now` IF
        `the Minister may lodge an instrument vesting the home in the Board` `the facts`
    AND `the section 8(4) notice requirements are met` `the facts`

-- s 8(5): on registration the title vests in the Board "WITHOUT FURTHER
-- ASSURANCE FREE FROM ALL ENCUMBRANCES", and the Registrar must cancel any
-- mortgage, charge or assurance overreached and any protecting caveat. The
-- mortgagee's security goes with it.
GIVEN `the instrument was registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any mortgage, charge or assurance is overreached and cancelled` IF
    `the instrument was registered`

§§ `10 -- The resale premium`

-- s 10: "Where any person who purchases any housing accommodation under the
-- executive condominium scheme had PREVIOUSLY PURCHASED, JOINTLY OR OTHERWISE,
-- any public housing accommodation from the Board, the person MUST pay to the
-- Board a premium of SUCH AMOUNT AS THE BOARD MAY DETERMINE."
--
-- A duty with no stated amount, no formula, no ceiling and no appeal. The
-- trigger is encodable; the quantum is not in the Act.
GIVEN `the person previously purchased public housing accommodation from the Board, jointly or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the person purchases housing under the executive condominium scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a premium is payable to the Board under section 10` IF
        `the person previously purchased public housing accommodation from the Board, jointly or otherwise`
    AND `the person purchases housing under the executive condominium scheme`

§§ `11 -- Service`

-- s 11(1): service is DEEMED effected if sent by registered post to the last
-- known address (or registered office or last known place of business), OR if
-- AFFIXED ON A CONSPICUOUS PART of the housing accommodation. Service by
-- registered letter is deemed made "at the time that such registered letter
-- would IN THE ORDINARY COURSE be delivered."
--
-- s 11(2): a notice to the owner is properly addressed if addressed to "THE
-- OWNER" of the accommodation "WITHOUT FURTHER NAME OR DESCRIPTION."
--
-- Read with s 5(4)'s 14-day appeal and s 8(4)'s 28-day notice, both of which
-- run from service: the clock can start on a notice pinned to the door and
-- addressed to nobody by name.
DECLARE ServiceMethod IS ONE OF
    `registered post to the last known address`                 -- (1)(a)
    `registered post to the registered office or last known place of business` -- (1)(b)
    `affixed on a conspicuous part of the housing accommodation` -- (1)(a) and (b)
    `some other method`

GIVEN `the method` IS A ServiceMethod
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service is deemed to have been effected` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `some other method` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the notice is addressed to "the owner" of the accommodation without further name or description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is properly addressed under section 11(2)` IF
    `the notice is addressed to "the owner" of the accommodation without further name or description`

§§ `12 -- Protection from liability`

-- s 12: "NO suit or other legal proceedings shall lie ... for or on account of
-- or in respect of anything which is IN GOOD FAITH done or intended to be done
-- by the Government, the Board, any public officer or other person acting under
-- the direction of the Minister in the execution or purported execution of this
-- Act."
--
-- GOOD FAITH ALONE. Compare s 19(1) of the Silver Support Scheme Act and s 19(1)
-- of the Advance Medical Directive Act, which both require good faith AND
-- reasonable care. Here a negligent but honest decision to vest someone's home
-- in the Board attracts no suit.
DECLARE ProtectedActor IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `the Board`
    `a public officer`
    `another person acting under the direction of the Minister`
    `someone outside the section 12 list`

GIVEN `the actor` IS A ProtectedActor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor is within the section 12 list` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `someone outside the section 12 list` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the actor` IS A ProtectedActor
    , `the act was done or intended in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the act was in the execution or purported execution of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no suit lies under section 12` IF
        `the actor is within the section 12 list` `the actor`
    AND `the act was done or intended in good faith`
    AND `the act was in the execution or purported execution of this Act`

§§ `13 -- Transfer to a non-citizen`

-- s 13(1): "DESPITE section 4 of the Residential Property Act 1976, a housing
-- accommodation under the executive condominium scheme MUST NOT be transferred
-- to any person who is NOT A CITIZEN OF SINGAPORE except in the following
-- circumstances ..."
--
-- The excepting circumstances follow in the text and turn on the Minister's
-- approval and on the period since the temporary occupation permit. They are
-- carried as one supplied fact rather than enumerated, because the deposited
-- text sets them out in a list this encoding did not read in full.
GIVEN `the transferee is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `a circumstance excepted by section 13(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is forbidden by section 13(1)` IF
        NOT `the transferee is a citizen of Singapore`
    AND NOT `a circumstance excepted by section 13(1) applies`
